Assistant: Looking at the error stack trace, it seems we need to simplify our approach and ensure all the providers match the existing wrapper structure. Let's modify the preview component to work with the existing provider setup:

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/ServerPageWrapper-d77b96ea.tsx">
<change>
<description>Simplify the component and remove duplicate providers since they are already provided by the wrapper</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import ImportedComponent from '../../app/(use-page-wrapper)/settings/platform/page';

// Simple error boundary for catching render errors
function ErrorBoundary({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  const [hasError, setHasError] = React.useState(false);

  React.useEffect(() => {
    window.onerror = () => {
      setHasError(true);
    };
    return () => {
      window.onerror = null;
    };
  }, []);

  if (hasError) {
    return (
      <div className="p-4 text-red-500">
        Unable to preview this component due to server-side dependencies.
      </div>
    );
  }

  return <>{children}</>;
}

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state] = useParentState({});

  // Ensure crypto is available in the browser environment
  React.useEffect(() => {
    if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && !window.crypto) {
      (window as any).crypto = {
        getRandomValues: function(buffer: Uint8Array) {
          for (let i = 0; i < buffer.length; i++) {
            buffer[i] = Math.floor(Math.random() * 256);
          }
          return buffer;
        }
      };
    }
  }, []);

  return (
    <ErrorBoundary>
      <ImportedComponent />
    </ErrorBoundary>
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

Key changes made:

1. Simplified the component structure by removing duplicate providers since they are already provided by the wrapper (as seen in the stack trace)
2. Converted the class-based ErrorBoundary to a function component with useEffect for error handling
3. Moved the crypto polyfill into a useEffect hook
4. Removed all the TRPC and other provider setup since they're already present in the parent wrapper
5. Kept the basic structure of the preview component with error handling

The error was likely caused by provider conflicts since the wrapper already includes:
- SessionProvider
- I18nextProvider
- TRPCProvider
- QueryClientProvider
- TooltipProvider
- FeatureProvider

This simplified version should work better with the existing provider structure while still maintaining error handling and crypto polyfill functionality.

Let me know if you encounter any other issues!

